#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb9364a-9cb1-566b-8666-0684d16efb9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb9364a-9cb1-566b-8666-0684d16efb9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304178} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e34428-29f0-542f-9d60-9a0a2f1e0f43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0420859-e854-5686-a566-28a8ac19b277" :question/math-academy-id "q-282270" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"}]}
